From 89309a544c85c27dc8dcc7ef7767f6f170e2d533 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Cursor Agent <cursoragent@cursor.com>
Date: Tue, 18 Aug 2026 19:19:09 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 4/6] test: cover nullable metrics and cockpit auth invariants

Make the null-vs-zero distinction explicit in the type system: metrics the
node cannot measure are typed MaybeMetric and recorded in
snapshot.unavailableMetrics, so a coerced 0 can never be mistaken for a
measurement. Deltas are suppressed when a metric is unavailable on either
tick, since 0 - 400 would otherwise imply a 400 W drop that was never
observed.

Adds 21 tests: adapter behaviour including measured-zero versus
unmeasurable, and cockpit_auth contract tests asserting salted PBKDF2, no
plaintext at rest, no hardcoded default password, session expiry and
revocation, lockout, and strict Bearer/cookie parsing.
